# Netlify header rules. Copied verbatim from public/ into dist/ by Astro.
#
# Astro fingerprints its own output under /_astro/, so Netlify already serves
# that immutably. public/fonts/*.woff2 are NOT fingerprinted — they were
# revalidating on every navigation under Netlify's default
# `cache-control: public,max-age=0,must-revalidate`, where fonts.gstatic.com
# had served the same bytes `immutable` for a year (Lighthouse
# `uses-long-cache-ttl` scored 0.5). The files are byte-frozen copies of a
# specific Google Fonts release; replacing one means a new filename, not a
# new revision of an existing one.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
